      "notes": "Executive summary; foundational framing of the tool."
    },
    {
      "id": "C-0002",
      "text": "On a Debian-bookworm Python 3.11 devcontainer, the canonical install path for Serena is `uvx --from git+https://github.com/oraios/serena serena start-mcp-server`.",
      "source_uri": "/workspaces/feature-pipeline/working/feature/devcontainer-mcp-provisioning-r1/research-notes/T-001-serena.md",
      "source_type": "community_blog",
      "source_provenance": "internal",
      "assumed_substrate": "claude_code",
      "date": "2026-05-23",
      "entities": [],
      "confidence": "high",
      "notes": "F-1 canonical install command (factual)."
    },
    {
      "id": "C-0003",
      "text": "The uv tool itself is the only required prerequisite for Serena installation; uv is managed by uvx as a subcommand.",
      "source_uri": "/workspaces/feature-pipeline/working/feature/devcontainer-mcp-provisioning-r1/research-notes/T-001-serena.md",
      "source_type": "community_blog",
      "source_provenance": "internal",
      "assumed_substrate": "claude_code",
      "date": "2026-05-23",
      "entities": [],
      "confidence": "high",
      "notes": "F-1 verbatim quote: 'Serena is managed by uv, and installing uv is the only required prerequisite.' (factual)"
    },
    {
      "id": "C-0004",
      "text": "An alternative install path is `uv tool install -p 3.13 serena-agent@latest --prerelease=allow` followed by invoking `serena` from PATH.",
      "source_uri": "/workspaces/feature-pipeline/working/feature/devcontainer-mcp-provisioning-r1/research-notes/T-001-serena.md",
      "source_type": "community_blog",
      "source_provenance": "internal",
      "assumed_substrate": "claude_code",
