      "source_type": "community_blog",
      "source_provenance": "internal",
      "assumed_substrate": "claude_code",
      "date": "2026-05-23",
      "entities": [],
      "confidence": "high",
      "notes": "F-6 (risk)."
    },
    {
      "id": "C-0042",
      "text": "Recommended pin is v1.5.1 (or whichever is latest-stable at integration time) by git tag for transparency, since the tag appears in the `.mcp.json` arg list and is visible in code review.",
      "source_uri": "/workspaces/feature-pipeline/working/feature/devcontainer-mcp-provisioning-r1/research-notes/T-001-serena.md",
      "source_type": "community_blog",
      "source_provenance": "internal",
      "assumed_substrate": "claude_code",
      "date": "2026-05-23",
      "entities": [],
      "confidence": "high",
      "notes": "F-6 (recommendation)."
    },
    {
      "id": "C-0043",
      "text": "Serena's value proposition is symbol-level code understanding built on Language Server Protocol backends per programming language.",
      "source_uri": "/workspaces/feature-pipeline/working/feature/devcontainer-mcp-provisioning-r1/research-notes/T-001-serena.md",
      "source_type": "community_blog",
      "source_provenance": "internal",
      "assumed_substrate": "claude_code",
      "date": "2026-05-23",
      "entities": [],
      "confidence": "high",
      "notes": "F-7 (factual)."
    },
    {
      "id": "C-0044",
      "text": "Serena's symbol-level tools (`find_symbol`, `find_referencing_symbols`, `replace_symbol_body`, `type_hierarchy`, `find_implementations`, etc.) are operations over declarations, references, and types as defined by an LSP server for a source language.",
      "source_uri": "/workspaces/feature-pipeline/working/feature/devcontainer-mcp-provisioning-r1/research-notes/T-001-serena.md",
      "source_type": "community_blog",
      "source_provenance": "internal",
      "assumed_substrate": "claude_code",
      "date": "2026-05-23",
      "entities": [],
      "confidence": "high",
      "notes": "F-7 (factual)."
    },
    {
      "id": "C-0045",
      "text": "Markdown is listed among Serena's 'supported languages' only in the broadest sense (the LSP ecosystem includes generic markdown servers for outline/link extraction), but upstream documentation provides no symbol-level capability listing for markdown.",
      "source_uri": "/workspaces/feature-pipeline/working/feature/devcontainer-mcp-provisioning-r1/research-notes/T-001-serena.md",
      "source_type": "community_blog",
      "source_provenance": "internal",
      "assumed_substrate": "claude_code",
      "date": "2026-05-23",
      "entities": [],
      "confidence": "high",
      "notes": "F-7 (factual)."
    },
    {
      "id": "C-0046",
      "text": "Serena's marketed value is uniformly framed around code (\"the IDE for your coding agent\").",
      "source_uri": "/workspaces/feature-pipeline/working/feature/devcontainer-mcp-provisioning-r1/research-notes/T-001-serena.md",
      "source_type": "community_blog",
      "source_provenance": "internal",
      "assumed_substrate": "claude_code",
      "date": "2026-05-23",
      "entities": [],
      "confidence": "high",
      "notes": "F-7 (factual)."
    },
    {
      "id": "C-0047",
      "text": "On a repo whose primary artifacts are markdown documents (specifications, KBs, PRDs, Plans, ADRs), Serena's symbol-level tools either return empty results or collapse to the basic-utility subset (`search_for_pattern`, `read_file`, `list_dir`, `find_file`).",
      "source_uri": "/workspaces/feature-pipeline/working/feature/devcontainer-mcp-provisioning-r1/research-notes/T-001-serena.md",
      "source_type": "community_blog",
      "source_provenance": "internal",
      "assumed_substrate": "claude_code",
      "date": "2026-05-23",
      "entities": [],
      "confidence": "high",
      "notes": "F-7 (factual/risk)."
    },
    {
      "id": "C-0048",
      "text": "Serena's basic-utility tools on markdown-dominant repos overlap heavily with Claude Code's native Read/Grep/Glob tools and provide no differentiation.",
      "source_uri": "/workspaces/feature-pipeline/working/feature/devcontainer-mcp-provisioning-r1/research-notes/T-001-serena.md",
      "source_type": "community_blog",
      "source_provenance": "internal",
      "assumed_substrate": "claude_code",
      "date": "2026-05-23",
      "entities": [],
      "confidence": "high",
      "notes": "F-7 (risk)."
    },
    {
      "id": "C-0049",
      "text": "On a markdown-dominant repository, the always-on token cost of Serena's tool descriptions is paid every session for capabilities the agent rarely uses and that duplicate native tools.",
      "source_uri": "/workspaces/feature-pipeline/working/feature/devcontainer-mcp-provisioning-r1/research-notes/T-001-serena.md",
      "source_type": "community_blog",
      "source_provenance": "internal",
      "assumed_substrate": "claude_code",
      "date": "2026-05-23",
      "entities": [],
      "confidence": "medium",
      "notes": "F-7 conclusion (risk/analyst synthesis flagged in source as medium-high)."
    },
    {
      "id": "C-0050",
      "text": "If the repository contains a non-trivial code subdirectory (e.g., audit Python scripts, validator scripts), Serena's symbol-level tools apply to that subdirectory.",
      "source_uri": "/workspaces/feature-pipeline/working/feature/devcontainer-mcp-provisioning-r1/research-notes/T-001-serena.md",
      "source_type": "community_blog",
      "source_provenance": "internal",
      "assumed_substrate": "claude_code",
      "date": "2026-05-23",
      "entities": [],
      "confidence": "high",
      "notes": "F-7 caveat (factual)."
    },
    {
      "id": "C-0051",
      "text": "A server-wide always-on Serena registration pays full context cost even when only a small applicable code subtree benefits.",
      "source_uri": "/workspaces/feature-pipeline/working/feature/devcontainer-mcp-provisioning-r1/research-notes/T-001-serena.md",
      "source_type": "community_blog",
      "source_provenance": "internal",
      "assumed_substrate": "claude_code",
      "date": "2026-05-23",
      "entities": [],
      "confidence": "high",
      "notes": "F-7 caveat (risk)."
    },
    {
      "id": "C-0052",
      "text": "Option 1 for Serena integration is always-on with broad `tools:` exposure, paying full context cost (estimate: tool-description overhead for ~20 tools is meaningful) where most tools are unused most of the time on a markdown-dominant repo.",
      "source_uri": "/workspaces/feature-pipeline/working/feature/devcontainer-mcp-provisioning-r1/research-notes/T-001-serena.md",
      "source_type": "community_blog",
      "source_provenance": "internal",
      "assumed_substrate": "claude_code",
      "date": "2026-05-23",
      "entities": [],
      "confidence": "high",
      "notes": "Synthesis option 1 (recommendation/trade-off)."
    },
    {
      "id": "C-0053",
      "text": "Option 2 for Serena integration is always-on with a narrowed `tools:` allowlist exposing only the basic-utility subset; this minimizes token-cost surface but eliminates Serena's differentiation versus Claude Code's native Read/Grep/Glob, making registration arguably redundant.",
      "source_uri": "/workspaces/feature-pipeline/working/feature/devcontainer-mcp-provisioning-r1/research-notes/T-001-serena.md",
      "source_type": "community_blog",
      "source_provenance": "internal",
      "assumed_substrate": "claude_code",
      "date": "2026-05-23",
      "entities": [],
      "confidence": "high",
      "notes": "Synthesis option 2 (recommendation/trade-off)."
    },
    {
      "id": "C-0054",
      "text": "Option 3 for Serena integration is to drop Serena from the always-on set and keep it as on-demand, since discovery-codebase-researcher is already served by GitNexus (primary) and codebase-memory-mcp (fallback) per ADR-0018 and KB-codebase-research/SKILL.md.",
      "source_uri": "/workspaces/feature-pipeline/working/feature/devcontainer-mcp-provisioning-r1/research-notes/T-001-serena.md",
      "source_type": "community_blog",
      "source_provenance": "internal",
